From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Sven Strickroth <email@cs-ware.de>
Date: Mon, 6 May 2013 16:06:20 -0400
Subject: We are a DLL, not a process

* Define exports of gitdll
* Do not use pager (also caused crashes in gitdll.dll in some cases)
* Add exit hook for gitdll - exit will cause program termination. Therefore, reimplimented by throw exception in TortoiseGit.
* Track all open file handles
* Do not print commits on STDOUT
* Do not try to fork or start sub processes, exit early before setting up handles and pipes
* Allow to schedule cleanup tasks
* Initialize critical sections and tracing
* chdir notify needs cleanup

Signed-off-by: Sven Strickroth <email@cs-ware.de>
Signed-off-by: Frank Li <lznuaa@gmail.com>
